<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.206 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.206 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.4 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due October 16 was 3.206 percent, up from 3.062 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.2 billion of 182-day T-bills due January 15, 1998 was 3.550 percent, up from 3.401 percent last week, and on C$1.0 billion of 357-day T-bills due July 9, 1998 was 4.162 percent, up from 3.897 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$525 million three-month, C$100 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$725 million of C$4.8 billion bills due July 24.</p>
